Single hold-out window: TSLM_log_how_hol (RMSE 87.8 )
Rolling origins       : TSLM_log_how_hol_tr (RMSE 89.94 , bias -5.49 )

The two protocols disagree, and the reason is visible in Figure F12: the
single window (18-31 December 2012) contains the Christmas collapse, when
demand fell to 441-1,000 rentals per day, i.e. far below any smooth annual
cycle. A model WITHOUT a trend has a lower level and is therefore rewarded
by that particular fortnight, even though the level of the series has risen
by about 42% between 2011 and 2012. Across 57 origins the version WITH a
linear trend is clearly better (RMSE89.94against115.7) and almost unbiased.
We therefore adoptTSLM_log_how_hol_tras the final model.

